  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Saturday)\nIssued at 211 PM EDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nThere are no big changes in expectations for the bulk of the \nextended forecast period that will bring hot and mostly dry \nconditions with any hope for a pattern change delayed until at least \nnext weekend. Above normal temperatures will peak during the midweek \ntime frame as the expansive upper ridge reaches its apex across the \nregion. Widespread highs in the mid 90s and heat index values near \nand over 100 degrees are expected. This will also serve to greatly \nlimit rain chances for the vast majority of the area with any \nappreciable chances for diurnal precipitation shunted to the far \nsouthern counties. \n\nAs mentioned above, hints of any pattern change will hold off until \nnext weekend when the upper ridge may retrograde westward, \npotentially setting up a trough across the eastern U.S. and allowing \na frontal boundary to push toward the area. This will also have a \nhand in determining the eventual track/evolution of the wave \nassociated with the remnants of former T.S. Dolly and its associated \nmoisture. Given this remains a week away, there is plenty of \nuncertainty in forecast details, so at this juncture PoPs gradually \nincrease by next weekend.",
